# Belt-and-braces deny list. The authoritative allowlist is `files` in package.json
# (dist/, README, LICENSE, SECURITY, hermes.config.example.yaml). This file
# ensures a stray untracked file at the repo root can't leak into the tarball.

# Source and test trees
src/
tests/
bench/
evals/
smoke/
artifacts/
coverage/

# Docs & site (published separately to GitHub Pages)
docs/
site/
HANDOFF.md
SHIP_GATE.md
SCORECARD.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Translated READMEs — NOTE: these lines are INERT and are kept only as a
# record of intent. npm-packlist force-includes anything matching README*
# regardless of `files` or this file, so all seven translations ship anyway.
# Measured 2026-09-11 on npm 10.9.8: `npm pack --dry-run --ignore-scripts`
# listed README.{es,fr,hi,it,ja,pt-BR,zh}.md (~420 kB of a 484 kB unpacked
# tarball) with these lines present AND with `files` omitting them. The only
# way to actually drop them is to move the files out of the package root
# (e.g. docs/i18n/) — a docs-domain change, not an ignore-file one.
README.es.md
README.fr.md
README.hi.md
README.it.md
README.ja.md
README.pt-BR.md
README.zh.md

# CI / repo config
.github/
.gitignore
.editorconfig
.polyglot-cache.json

# Build / test config
tsconfig.json
tsconfig*.json
vitest.config.*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test files anywhere in the tree
*.test.*
*.spec.*

# hermes.config.example.yaml is SHIPPED on purpose (package.json `files`).
# It used to be denied here as "not needed at runtime", which was wrong: the
# advertised `init` verb copies it out of the package root
# (src/index.ts resolves <bin-dir>/../hermes.config.example.yaml), so with the
# file absent every npm install answered `init` with its own "This is a
# packaging bug" error. `files` wins over .npmignore, but a deny line that
# contradicts the allowlist is a trap for the next reader, so it is gone
# rather than merely overridden. The tarball install-and-run smoke in
# ci.yml's lockfile-sync job is what keeps this honest.

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tgz
.env
.env.local
